Saoirse (given name):
Saoirse (
Irish: [ˈsˠiːɾˠʃə] ;
anglicised /ˈsɪərʃə/, /ˈsɛərʃə/, or /ˈsɜːrʃə/
) is an Irish-language unisex given name meaning "freedom". It became popular in Ireland in the late 20th century. The actress Saoirse Ronan has given the name prominence internationally since her 2007 breakthrough in Atonement.
